# Tests — FY26 Sales Commission Plan: commission earned

Assertion-based tests for `Commission`. Every branch of every exception
hierarchy is covered, and every numeric threshold is tested on both sides of
the boundary, because the Plan's own comparison operators are not uniform:
S-4.1 uses "or more" (inclusive) at the foot of each band and "less than"
(exclusive) at the head, S-4.3 and S-5.3 use "more than" and "exceeds"
(strict), S-2.4 uses "within 180 days" (inclusive) and S-8.1 uses "on or
before" (inclusive). A single mid-range test sees none of that.

Four traps get dedicated tests that assert a *difference* rather than only a
value, because the wrong encoding of each produces a perfectly plausible
number: S-4.2 (the accelerator is a cliff over the whole of Net Booked
Revenue, not a marginal rate), S-5.2 (the cap comes after the accelerator, not
before), S-4.4 (the joiner cap defeats S-4.1 as well as S-4.3) and S-2.2 (the
Quota it divides by is exact, so a sub-penny relieved Quota cannot be rounded
across an S-4.1 band boundary — CE-0027).

The last section covers the nil Quota S-6.1 can produce (CE-0026). It is an
input the Plan compels and `Attainment` answers for it; the guard that used to
refuse it refused nothing, because the quotient was evaluated first and raised
a division by zero.

> Using Commission

## Contract fixtures

Constructors for the `Commission.Contract` records the tests need. They carry
no law; they exist so that a test reads as the fact pattern it is.

```catala
declaration signed_only content Commission.Contract
  depends on
    id content integer,
    acv content money,
    signed content date,
    prior content list of date
  equals
    Commission.Contract {
      -- contract_id: id
      -- annual_contract_value: acv
      -- signature_date: signed
      -- terminated_by_customer_on: Absent
      -- not_renewed_at_first_renewal_on: Absent
      -- customer_contract_dates: prior
    }

declaration terminated_on content Commission.Contract
  depends on
    id content integer,
    acv content money,
    signed content date,
    prior content list of date,
    event content date
  equals
    (signed_only of id, acv, signed, prior)
    but replace { -- terminated_by_customer_on: Present content event }

declaration not_renewed_on content Commission.Contract
  depends on
    id content integer,
    acv content money,
    signed content date,
    prior content list of date,
    event content date
  equals
    (signed_only of id, acv, signed, prior)
    but replace { -- not_renewed_at_first_renewal_on: Present content event }
```

## S-1.1 The Plan Year window

A contract signed on the first day of the Plan Year is in; one signed the day
before is out. The window is inclusive at both ends.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS1_1_PlanYearBoundaries:
  output r content Commission.NetBookedRevenue

scope TestS1_1_PlanYearBoundaries:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NetBookedRevenue with {
      -- contracts: [
           signed_only of 1, $100,000, |2025-09-30|, [|2025-01-01|];
           signed_only of 2, $200,000, |2025-10-01|, [|2025-01-01|];
           signed_only of 3, $400,000, |2026-09-30|, [|2025-01-01|];
           signed_only of 4, $800,000, |2026-10-01|, [|2025-01-01|]
         ]
    }
  assertion r.gross_booked_revenue = $600,000
  assertion r.net_booked_revenue = $600,000
```

## S-2.1 Quota assignment date

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_1_QuotaAtPlanYearStart:
  output r content Commission.AssignedQuota

scope TestS2_1_QuotaAtPlanYearStart:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.AssignedQuota with {
      -- assigned_quota: $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2020-04-01|
    }
  assertion r.quota_assignment_date = |2025-10-01|
  assertion r.quota = $1,000,000
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_1_QuotaOnJoiningIfLater:
  output r content Commission.AssignedQuota

scope TestS2_1_QuotaOnJoiningIfLater:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.AssignedQuota with {
      -- assigned_quota: $400,000
      -- commencement_date: |2026-01-15|
    }
  assertion r.quota_assignment_date = |2026-01-15|
  assertion r.quota = $400,000
```

## S-2.4 Churned Contract — the 180-day boundary

2025-10-01 plus 180 days is 2026-03-30. An event on that day is within the
window; an event the next day is not.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_4_TerminatedOnDay180:
  output r content Commission.ChurnedContract

scope TestS2_4_TerminatedOnDay180:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.ChurnedContract with {
      -- contract: terminated_on of 1, $100,000, |2025-10-01|, [], |2026-03-30|
    }
  assertion r.is_churned = true
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_4_TerminatedOnDay181:
  output r content Commission.ChurnedContract

scope TestS2_4_TerminatedOnDay181:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.ChurnedContract with {
      -- contract: terminated_on of 1, $100,000, |2025-10-01|, [], |2026-03-31|
    }
  assertion r.is_churned = false
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_4_NotRenewedOnDay180:
  output r content Commission.ChurnedContract

scope TestS2_4_NotRenewedOnDay180:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.ChurnedContract with {
      -- contract: not_renewed_on of 1, $100,000, |2025-10-01|, [], |2026-03-30|
    }
  assertion r.is_churned = true
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_4_NotRenewedOnDay181:
  output r content Commission.ChurnedContract

scope TestS2_4_NotRenewedOnDay181:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.ChurnedContract with {
      -- contract: not_renewed_on of 1, $100,000, |2025-10-01|, [], |2026-03-31|
    }
  assertion r.is_churned = false
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_4_NoChurnEvent:
  output r content Commission.ChurnedContract

scope TestS2_4_NoChurnEvent:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.ChurnedContract with {
      -- contract: signed_only of 1, $100,000, |2025-10-01|, []
    }
  assertion r.is_churned = false
```

An event dated before signature is not a churn event: the 180-day window opens
at signature and runs forward.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_4_EventBeforeSignature:
  output r content Commission.ChurnedContract

scope TestS2_4_EventBeforeSignature:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.ChurnedContract with {
      -- contract: terminated_on of 1, $100,000, |2025-10-01|, [], |2025-09-01|
    }
  assertion r.is_churned = false
```

## S-2.6 New Logo — the 24-month window

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_6_NoPriorContract:
  output r content Commission.NewLogo

scope TestS2_6_NoPriorContract:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NewLogo with {
      -- signature_date: |2026-01-01|
      -- customer_contract_dates: []
    }
  assertion r.window_start = |2024-01-01|
  assertion r.is_new_logo = true
```

A prior contract on the first day of the window disqualifies: the window is
inclusive at its far end.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_6_PriorAtWindowStart:
  output r content Commission.NewLogo

scope TestS2_6_PriorAtWindowStart:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NewLogo with {
      -- signature_date: |2026-01-01|
      -- customer_contract_dates: [|2024-01-01|]
    }
  assertion r.window_start = |2024-01-01|
  assertion r.is_new_logo = false
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_6_PriorOneDayBeforeWindow:
  output r content Commission.NewLogo

scope TestS2_6_PriorOneDayBeforeWindow:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NewLogo with {
      -- signature_date: |2026-01-01|
      -- customer_contract_dates: [|2023-12-31|]
    }
  assertion r.is_new_logo = true
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_6_PriorInsideWindow:
  output r content Commission.NewLogo

scope TestS2_6_PriorInsideWindow:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NewLogo with {
      -- signature_date: |2026-01-01|
      -- customer_contract_dates: [|2025-06-01|]
    }
  assertion r.is_new_logo = false
```

The contract under test cannot disqualify itself: the window is the 24 months
*preceding* the signature date, so the signature date itself is excluded.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_6_PriorOnSignatureDate:
  output r content Commission.NewLogo

scope TestS2_6_PriorOnSignatureDate:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NewLogo with {
      -- signature_date: |2026-01-01|
      -- customer_contract_dates: [|2026-01-01|]
    }
  assertion r.is_new_logo = true
```

## S-2.3 Net Booked Revenue is net of churn

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_3_NetOfChurnedContracts:
  output r content Commission.NetBookedRevenue

scope TestS2_3_NetOfChurnedContracts:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NetBookedRevenue with {
      -- contracts: [
           signed_only of 1, $1,500,000, |2026-01-01|, [|2025-06-01|];
           terminated_on of 2, $500,000, |2026-01-01|, [|2025-06-01|], |2026-02-01|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.gross_booked_revenue = $2,000,000
  assertion r.churned_contract_value = $500,000
  assertion r.net_booked_revenue = $1,500,000
```

## S-4.3 first limb — the New Logo share of Net Booked Revenue

A churned contract counts in neither the numerator nor the denominator: it is
not part of Net Booked Revenue at all.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_3_NewLogoShareExcludesChurn:
  output r content Commission.NetBookedRevenue

scope TestS4_3_NewLogoShareExcludesChurn:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NetBookedRevenue with {
      -- contracts: [
           signed_only of 1, $600,000, |2026-01-01|, [];
           signed_only of 2, $400,000, |2026-01-01|, [|2025-06-01|];
           terminated_on of 3, $300,000, |2026-01-01|, [], |2026-02-01|
         ]
    }
  assertion r.net_booked_revenue = $1,000,000
  assertion r.new_logo_revenue = $600,000
  assertion r.new_logo_share = 60%
```

A nil Net Booked Revenue yields a nil share rather than a division by zero.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_3_NewLogoShareOnNilRevenue:
  output r content Commission.NetBookedRevenue

scope TestS4_3_NewLogoShareOnNilRevenue:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.NetBookedRevenue with { -- contracts: [] }
  assertion r.net_booked_revenue = $0
  assertion r.new_logo_share = 0.0
```

## S-2.2 Attainment

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_2_Attainment:
  output r content Commission.Attainment

scope TestS2_2_Attainment:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Attainment with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $1,500,000
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
    }
  assertion r.attainment_pct = 150%
```

## S-4.1 The accelerator bands, on both sides of every threshold

`commencement_date` of 2025-10-01 is the first day of the Plan Year, so these
employees did not commence *after* the start of the Plan Year and S-4.4 does
not engage.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_1_Below50:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_1_Below50:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 49.99%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.s4_1_band = 0.0
  assertion r.accelerator = 0.0
  assertion r.commenced_after_plan_year_start = false
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_1_Exactly50:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_1_Exactly50:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 50%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.s4_1_band = 1.0
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.0
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_1_JustUnder100:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_1_JustUnder100:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 99.99%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.0
```

100% is "100% or more", so it belongs to band (c) and not to band (b). This is
the boundary a marginal-rate reading gets wrong.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_1_Exactly100:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_1_Exactly100:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 100%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.5
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_1_JustUnder150:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_1_JustUnder150:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 149.99%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.5
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_1_Exactly150:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_1_Exactly150:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 150%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator = 2.0
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_1_WellAbove150:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_1_WellAbove150:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 300%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator = 2.0
```

## S-4.3 The New Logo uplift — "more than 60%" is strict

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_3_ShareExactly60:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_3_ShareExactly60:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 150%
      -- new_logo_share: 60%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.s4_1_band = 2.0
  assertion r.accelerator_before_joiner_cap = 2.0
  assertion r.accelerator = 2.0
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_3_ShareJustOver60:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_3_ShareJustOver60:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 150%
      -- new_logo_share: 60.01%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator_before_joiner_cap = 2.25
  assertion r.accelerator = 2.25
```

The uplift is 0.25 on whatever band S-4.1 produced, so it lifts band (b) as
well as band (d).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_3_UpliftOnBandB:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_3_UpliftOnBandB:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 60%
      -- new_logo_share: 70%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.s4_1_band = 1.0
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.25
```

S-4.3 is unconditional as to band, so on the literal text it lifts band (a) —
a sub-50% attainer — from 0.0 to 0.25. The Plan does not say the uplift is
available only where commission is otherwise earned, and this test pins the
literal reading so that a change of mind about it shows up as a test failure
rather than as a silent drift.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_3_UpliftOnBandA:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_3_UpliftOnBandA:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 40%
      -- new_logo_share: 70%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.s4_1_band = 0.0
  assertion r.accelerator = 0.25
```

## S-4.4 The mid-year joiner cap

"Commenced after the start of the Plan Year" is strict: an employee whose
first day is 1 October 2025 is not a mid-year joiner.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_4_CommencedOnPlanYearStart:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_4_CommencedOnPlanYearStart:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 150%
      -- new_logo_share: 70%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
    }
  assertion r.commenced_after_plan_year_start = false
  assertion r.accelerator = 2.25
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_4_CommencedDayAfterPlanYearStart:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_4_CommencedDayAfterPlanYearStart:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 150%
      -- new_logo_share: 70%
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-02|
    }
  assertion r.commenced_after_plan_year_start = true
  assertion r.accelerator_before_joiner_cap = 2.25
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.5
```

S-4.4 is an exception to S-4.1 as well as to S-4.3. A joiner with no New Logo
uplift at all must still be capped: were the joiner cap to inherit S-4.3's
"more than 60%" condition, this employee would keep the uncapped 2.0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_4_JoinerCapDefeatsS4_1Alone:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_4_JoinerCapDefeatsS4_1Alone:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 150%
      -- new_logo_share: 30%
      -- commencement_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.s4_1_band = 2.0
  assertion r.accelerator_before_joiner_cap = 2.0
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.5
```

The cap is a ceiling, not a fixed value: where the otherwise applicable
accelerator is below 1.5 the joiner keeps it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_4_JoinerCapInertBelowCeiling:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_4_JoinerCapInertBelowCeiling:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 60%
      -- new_logo_share: 30%
      -- commencement_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.0
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_4_JoinerCapInertWithUplift:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_4_JoinerCapInertWithUplift:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 60%
      -- new_logo_share: 70%
      -- commencement_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator_before_joiner_cap = 1.25
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.25
```

A joiner exactly at the ceiling is unaffected: band (c) is 1.5 already.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_4_JoinerAtCeiling:
  output r content Commission.Accelerator

scope TestS4_4_JoinerAtCeiling:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Accelerator with {
      -- attainment_pct: 100%
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- commencement_date: |2026-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.accelerator = 1.5
```

## S-4.2 The accelerator applies to the whole of Net Booked Revenue

Attainment of 120% puts the employee in band (c), accelerator 1.5. On the
Plan's reading the whole of Net Booked Revenue is accelerated:
$1,200,000 x 8.0% x 1.5 = $144,000. On the marginal reading rejected by S-4.2
the accelerator would apply only to the $200,000 above the 100% threshold:
$1,000,000 x 8.0% x 1.0 + $200,000 x 8.0% x 1.5 = $104,000. The test asserts
the first figure and asserts that it is not the second.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS4_2_WholeRevenueNotMarginal:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS4_2_WholeRevenueNotMarginal:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $1,200,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $200,000
    }
  assertion r.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 120%
  assertion r.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 1.5
  assertion r.accelerator_base = $1,200,000
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $144,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $144,000
  assertion r.commission_payable
    != ($1,000,000 * 8.0% * 1.0) + ($200,000 * 8.0% * 1.5)
```

## S-3.1 A nil Net Booked Revenue yields nil commission

The joiner cap is inert at the foot of the band table too, and nil revenue
yields nil commission whatever the accelerator. This is why S-4.4's literal
test needs no upper bound on the commencement date: an employee who commenced
after the Plan Year ended has no Plan Year revenue to accelerate.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS3_1_NilRevenueNilCommission:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS3_1_NilRevenueNilCommission:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $0
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2026-11-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 0%
  assertion r.accelerator_calc.commenced_after_plan_year_start = true
  assertion r.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 0.0
  assertion r.accelerator_base = $0
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $0
  assertion r.commission_payable = $0
```

## S-3.1 One product, one rounding — CE-0015

S-3.1 prescribes a single product of three factors. Because `money` is fixed at
the cent, computing Net Booked Revenue x the Base Commission Rate first rounds
an intermediate that the accelerator then magnifies. On Net Booked Revenue of
$10,000.44 against a Quota of $8,000 — Attainment 125.0055%, band (c),
accelerator 1.5 — the product is $10,000.44 x 0.12 = $1,200.0528, which is
$1,200.05 to the cent on any rounding rule, because the remainder is 0.28 of a
cent. The two-step form paid $1,200.06.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS3_1_NoIntermediateRoundingAt1_5:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS3_1_NoIntermediateRoundingAt1_5:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $10,000.44
      -- new_logo_share: 10%
      -- quota: decimal of $8,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 1.250055
  assertion r.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 1.5
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $1,200.05
  assertion r.commission_payable = $1,200.05
  assertion r.commission_payable != $1,200.06
```

The error is systematic across accelerators, so the same revenue is tested at
1.75 (S-4.3 engaged by a 70% New Logo share): $10,000.44 x 0.08 x 1.75 =
$1,400.0616, so $1,400.06 and not the $1,400.07 the two-step form produced.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS3_1_NoIntermediateRoundingAt1_75:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS3_1_NoIntermediateRoundingAt1_75:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $10,000.44
      -- new_logo_share: 70%
      -- quota: decimal of $8,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 1.75
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $1,400.06
  assertion r.commission_payable = $1,400.06
  assertion r.commission_payable != $1,400.07
```

And at 2.25 — band (d) plus the S-4.3 uplift, on a Quota of $5,000 which puts
Attainment at 200.0088% and so raises the cap to 400% under S-5.3:
$10,000.44 x 0.08 x 2.25 = $1,800.0792, so $1,800.08 and not $1,800.09.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS3_1_NoIntermediateRoundingAt2_25:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS3_1_NoIntermediateRoundingAt2_25:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $10,000.44
      -- new_logo_share: 70%
      -- quota: decimal of $5,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 2.25
  assertion r.cap = $400,000
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $1,800.08
  assertion r.commission_payable = $1,800.08
  assertion r.commission_payable != $1,800.09
```

## S-5.1 The 250% cap

Where the cap does not bite, the capped figure is the uncapped one.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS5_1_CapNotBinding:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS5_1_CapNotBinding:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $1,000,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $200,000
    }
  assertion r.cap = $500,000
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $120,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $120,000
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS5_1_CapBinding:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS5_1_CapBinding:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $3,000,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $2,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.cap = $250,000
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $480,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $250,000
```

## S-5.2 The cap is applied after the accelerator

The same fact pattern, asserting the *order*. Applying the cap first —
capping $3,000,000 x 8.0% = $240,000 at $250,000, which leaves it untouched,
and then accelerating by 2.0 — yields $480,000. The Plan's order yields
$250,000. Both are arithmetically tidy; only one is the Plan's.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS5_2_CapAfterAcceleratorNotBefore:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS5_2_CapAfterAcceleratorNotBefore:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $3,000,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $2,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 2.0
  assertion r.commission_payable = $250,000
  assertion (Money.min of ($3,000,000 * 8.0%), $250,000) * 2.0 = $480,000
  assertion r.commission_payable
    != (Money.min of ($3,000,000 * 8.0%), $250,000) * 2.0
```

## S-5.3 The 400% cap — "exceeds 200%" is strict

Attainment of exactly 200% keeps the 250% cap.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS5_3_AttainmentExactly200:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS5_3_AttainmentExactly200:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $2,000,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 200%
  assertion r.cap = $250,000
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $320,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $250,000
```

Attainment above 200% raises the cap to 400%, and the employee keeps the
figure the 250% cap would have taken away.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS5_3_AttainmentAbove200:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS5_3_AttainmentAbove200:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $2,100,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 210%
  assertion r.cap = $400,000
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $336,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $336,000
  assertion r.commission_payable != $250,000
```

The raised cap can still bite.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS5_3_RaisedCapStillBinds:
  output r content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS5_3_RaisedCapStillBinds:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $10,000,000
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
    }
  assertion r.cap = $400,000
  assertion r.commission_before_cap = $1,600,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $400,000
```

## S-8.1 Leavers — the cut-off is "on or before" the last day

The contract signed on the last day of employment qualifies; the one signed
afterwards does not. Attainment of $1,000,000 against a $1,000,000 quota is
100%, band (c), so commission is $1,000,000 x 8.0% x 1.5 = $120,000, of which
$20,000 has been paid.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS8_1_LeaverCutOffInclusive:
  output r content Commission.LeaverCommission

scope TestS8_1_LeaverCutOffInclusive:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.LeaverCommission with {
      -- contracts: [
           signed_only of 1, $1,000,000, |2026-01-01|, [|2025-06-01|];
           signed_only of 2, $500,000, |2026-06-01|, [|2025-06-01|]
         ]
      -- last_day_of_employment: |2026-01-01|
      -- termination_reason: OtherReason
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
      -- commission_already_paid: $20,000
    }
  assertion number of r.qualifying_contracts = 1
  assertion r.revenue.net_booked_revenue = $1,000,000
  assertion r.entitlement.commission_before_cap = $120,000
  assertion r.entitlement.commission_payable = $120,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $100,000
```

Moving the last day one day earlier excludes the contract entirely.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS8_1_LeaverCutOffExcludesLater:
  output r content Commission.LeaverCommission

scope TestS8_1_LeaverCutOffExcludesLater:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.LeaverCommission with {
      -- contracts: [
           signed_only of 1, $1,000,000, |2026-01-01|, [|2025-06-01|];
           signed_only of 2, $500,000, |2026-06-01|, [|2025-06-01|]
         ]
      -- last_day_of_employment: |2025-12-31|
      -- termination_reason: OtherReason
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
      -- commission_already_paid: $0
    }
  assertion number of r.qualifying_contracts = 0
  assertion r.revenue.net_booked_revenue = $0
  assertion r.entitlement.commission_payable = $0
  assertion r.commission_payable = $0
```

## S-8.2 Gross misconduct forfeits the unpaid balance

Same fact pattern as `TestS8_1_LeaverCutOffInclusive`: the entitlement is
unchanged at $120,000 and $20,000 has been paid, but the $100,000 balance is
forfeited.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS8_2_GrossMisconductForfeitsBalance:
  output r content Commission.LeaverCommission

scope TestS8_2_GrossMisconductForfeitsBalance:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.LeaverCommission with {
      -- contracts: [
           signed_only of 1, $1,000,000, |2026-01-01|, [|2025-06-01|];
           signed_only of 2, $500,000, |2026-06-01|, [|2025-06-01|]
         ]
      -- last_day_of_employment: |2026-01-01|
      -- termination_reason: GrossMisconduct
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $100,000
      -- commission_already_paid: $20,000
    }
  assertion r.entitlement.commission_payable = $120,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $0
```

## S-8.1 An overpayment is not a debt — CE-0016

A leaver whose entitlement is $140,000 and who has already been paid $200,000
through an administrative error is owed nothing, and owes nothing under this
Plan. No contract has churned, so S-7.1 — the Plan's only recovery power, and
one fenced by S-7.2 and S-7.3 — cannot operate at all, and a negative
`commission_payable` would assert a debt the Plan does not create. The $60,000
is reported as `overpaid_amount` instead: a fact, not an entitlement either way.

One contract of $1,000,000 signed on the last day of employment, a New Logo
customer (so the S-4.3 uplift applies to the 100% share), Quota $1,000,000 and
salary $500,000: $1,000,000 x 8.0% x 1.75 = $140,000, inside the 250% cap.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS8_1_OverpaymentIsNotADebt:
  output r content Commission.LeaverCommission

scope TestS8_1_OverpaymentIsNotADebt:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.LeaverCommission with {
      -- contracts: [ signed_only of 1, $1,000,000, |2026-03-31|, [] ]
      -- last_day_of_employment: |2026-03-31|
      -- termination_reason: OtherReason
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $500,000
      -- commission_already_paid: $200,000
    }
  assertion r.entitlement.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 1.75
  assertion r.entitlement.commission_payable = $140,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $0
  assertion r.commission_payable >= $0
  assertion r.commission_payable != -$60,000
  assertion r.overpaid_amount = $60,000
```

The floor is inside the S-8.1 expression rather than an exception to it. Were it
an exception it would be a sibling of `s8_2`, and an overpaid gross-misconduct
leaver would satisfy both conditions and raise a `Conflict`. This test is that
leaver, and it answers.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS8_2_OverpaidGrossMisconductLeaver:
  output r content Commission.LeaverCommission

scope TestS8_2_OverpaidGrossMisconductLeaver:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.LeaverCommission with {
      -- contracts: [ signed_only of 1, $1,000,000, |2026-03-31|, [] ]
      -- last_day_of_employment: |2026-03-31|
      -- termination_reason: GrossMisconduct
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $500,000
      -- commission_already_paid: $200,000
    }
  assertion r.entitlement.commission_payable = $140,000
  assertion r.commission_payable = $0
  assertion r.overpaid_amount = $60,000
```

Where the entitlement exceeds what has been paid, nothing is floored and
nothing is reported as overpaid.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS8_1_NoOverpaymentReportedWhenUnderpaid:
  output r content Commission.LeaverCommission

scope TestS8_1_NoOverpaymentReportedWhenUnderpaid:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.LeaverCommission with {
      -- contracts: [ signed_only of 1, $1,000,000, |2026-03-31|, [] ]
      -- last_day_of_employment: |2026-03-31|
      -- termination_reason: OtherReason
      -- quota: decimal of $1,000,000
      -- commencement_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $500,000
      -- commission_already_paid: $40,000
    }
  assertion r.commission_payable = $100,000
  assertion r.overpaid_amount = $0
```

## S-2.2 A nil Quota is answered, not refused — CE-0026

S-6.1 reduces the Quota to nil where a qualifying absence covers every day of
the Plan Year, so a nil Quota is an input the Plan produces and `Attainment`
must answer for it rather than dividing by zero. The nil-Quota limb reports 0%,
which carries through S-4.1(a) to an accelerator of 0.0 and, on the nil Net
Booked Revenue that accompanies it, to the $0.00 S-3.1 fixes whatever the
accelerator.

The two refusals the scope keeps are error cases and so cannot be asserted
here: executed with a nil Quota and a *positive* Net Booked Revenue, and with a
negative Quota, the scope reports `AssertionFailed` — a percentage of nothing
is not a quantity the Plan fixes, and there is no such thing as a negative
Quota. Both were verified by execution; neither is reachable through
`QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief`.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_2_NilQuotaGivesNilAttainment:
  output r content Commission.Attainment
  output payable content Commission.CommissionPayable

scope TestS2_2_NilQuotaGivesNilAttainment:
  definition r equals
    output of Commission.Attainment with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $0
      -- quota: 0.0
    }

  definition payable equals
    output of Commission.CommissionPayable with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $0
      -- new_logo_share: 0%
      -- quota: 0.0
      -- commencement_date: |2020-01-01|
      -- annual_base_salary: $120,000
    }

  assertion r.attainment_pct = 0%
  assertion payable.attainment_calc.attainment_pct = 0%
  assertion payable.accelerator_calc.accelerator = 0.0
  assertion payable.commission_before_cap = $0
  assertion payable.commission_payable = $0
```

## S-2.2 The denominator is exact, so a sub-penny Quota does not move a band — CE-0027

The Quota is taken as an exact `decimal` because S-6.1's relief is 1/365ths of
an annual figure and so is not in general a whole number of pence. On
$344,178.08 of Net Booked Revenue the exact relieved Quota of
$688,356.1643835616... gives Attainment below 50%, and the same Quota rounded to
the penny gives exactly 50% — which is the S-4.1(a)/(b) boundary, 0.0 against
1.0. The pair is the test.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS2_2_ExactDenominatorKeepsTheBand:
  output exact content Commission.Attainment
  output rounded content Commission.Attainment

scope TestS2_2_ExactDenominatorKeepsTheBand:
  definition exact equals
    output of Commission.Attainment with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $344,178.08
      -- quota: 750000.0 - 750000.0 * (30.0 / 365.0)
    }

  definition rounded equals
    output of Commission.Attainment with {
      -- net_booked_revenue: $344,178.08
      -- quota: decimal of $688,356.16
    }

  assertion exact.attainment_pct < 50%
  assertion exact.attainment_pct != 50%
  assertion rounded.attainment_pct = 50%
  assertion exact.attainment_pct != rounded.attainment_pct
```
